\f1\fs22 In the pre-dawn darkness of a long sunny Wednesday on the twenty-third of a December, the Ulyssian Defence Force deployed a forward contingent of ordnance and troops to knock on Eloise Shakti\'92s Sublime Point front door.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 While the gate to the compound was open, most who knew the place understood that open did not imply invitation. The first to set foot on Shakti gravel received a particle-beam-sized hole in his army-issue left boot. He and the rest of his fire team learned how vaporised wool and toes irritated the nostrils, and abandoned the door-knock. They weren\'92t serious anyway; they were just testing if Sublime Point\'92s feared weapons array was spending the night at home.\
\'93Fall back!\'94 one of the team ordered after the toe-holed mate had done exactly that.\
Other fire teams and sections, that were arranged back along the access road and through the bush on the northern perimeter of the compound, were urged to exercise caution and await further orders.\
Major Midler of the UDF made several attempts to set up a command post and was met with local resistance in the form of legal teams, having been summoned from their beds and favourite night clubs to wave restraining orders and declare that camouflage tents, artillery and jack boots were not in keeping with village character. Eventually, Midler signed in to Airborne Bed\'92n\'92Banquet, and booked a backyard pool house by the golf course, although accepting the terms and conditions irked him, especially the clause forbidding cigar-smoking while swimming in the pool.\
Communications gear was still being loaded in when a contingent of residents marched on the pool house\'97some still in night gowns, others accompanied by their poodles and wolfhounds\'97and demanded to see every soldier\'92s working with children check. Another contingent arrived and demanded to know the meaning of the incursion, and then ruled Major Midler\'92s reply as out of order for discussing military matters. Others demanded to know if the major worked for a private army or the communist government one. Others threatened to commission an acoustic analysis and said that, while they didn\'92t mind the sound of gunshot, they would not abide idling trucks in their streets. Others threatened that hindrance of council vehicles\'92 access to garbage bins would be met with the kind of litigation that would send Major Midler\'92s ancestors broke. Wolfhounds and 
\f2\i shih tzus
\f1\i0  barked happily about that. One resident showed up with a bleary-eyed lawyer, and demanded to see the prospectus and an application form to invest. A patrician resident arrived in slippers and a cat sleeping in her hair. While both the old woman and the indeterminately aged cat looked unhappy, neither spoke a word.\
The sun hadn\'92t come up yet. At least 
\f2\i it
\f1\i0  wasn\'92t complaining.\
Major Midler ordered troops to hold positions. Inevitably, some small skirmishes occurred between a few ill-disciplined UDF deployments and Shakti technology. None of the UDF got a shot off, though Shakti defences sizzled ground cover, brought down eucalyptus branches and melted neat holes through bush rock. A surveillance camera in one soldier\'92s pack turned to hot slag, delivering no more than a warm tickle before the soldier had slung the pack to the ground.\
Major Midler ordered reconnaissance drones.\
One crossed a boundary only Shakti defences appeared able to see and became fireworks. A second moved low through the trees and exploded, startling a cuddle of koalas. Another climbed, circled and survived long enough to transmit several seconds of excellent landscape footage  suitable for a tourism campaign before bits of it went off to explore different parts of the ground cover. In the command centre pool house, Major Midler\'92s officers went back to their maps on tablets as big as atlases, and reported they had \'93taken\'94 the fifty-odd hectares of bush area between the golf course and the Shakti compound. The major thought rather, they had been allowed to take it.\
Stripped of acronyms and optimism, Major Midler framed his own sit-rep. He could probably take the place, but he wasn\'92t going to enjoy it.\
As the sun came up, he lit his first cigar and flicked ashes into the pool.
